Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.41,0:02:25.22,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,The Second Law of Thermodynamics:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.77,0:02:28.64,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,Heat can never pass from \Na colder to a warmer body
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.64,0:02:30.40,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,without causing other effects,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.27,0:02:35.01,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,or it is impossible to convert heat \Nfrom a single source into work
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.01,0:02:36.78,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,without causing other effects,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.93,0:02:41.98,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,or entropy always increases in \Nan irreversible heat reaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.76,0:02:46.34,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,Escaping the burden of an entropy increase
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.34,0:02:48.33,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,and to create something from nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.33,0:02:50.14,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,The witch's power is truly convenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.71,0:02:54.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.70,0:03:00.70,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Good morning, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.88,0:03:02.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.38,0:03:05.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Did you do what I asked?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.20,0:03:06.85,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,It's done, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.24,0:03:09.52,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The witch was hanged at noon.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.52,0:03:11.02,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The prisoner wore a hood,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.02,0:03:12.96,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,so no one noticed anything unusual.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.96,0:03:14.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Okay, very good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.77,0:03:16.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Next, prepare some data for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.85,0:03:18.85,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Yes. What do you need?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.34,0:03:22.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I need a report summarizing \NBorder Town's trade,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.11,0:03:24.96,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,taxes, and fixed expenditures \Nfor the past decade.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.96,0:03:26.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Also, let me think...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.33,0:03:30.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,For the workshops in the town,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.85,0:03:33.07,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,such as ironworks, textiles, and pottery,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.07,0:03:34.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,compile statistics on \Ntheir numbers and scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.80,0:03:36.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and give me a detailed report.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.60,0:03:38.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Include the population distribution and
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.65,0:03:40.07,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,occupations in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.65,0:03:40.07,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.85,0:03:42.65,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,what do you need those for?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.51,0:03:45.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Don't worry. Just give them to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.72,0:03:47.37,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.37,0:03:51.26,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, are you finally \Ntaking the Royal Decree seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.42,0:03:53.96,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Royal Decree?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.10,0:04:02.02,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,COLDWIND RIDGE
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.50,0:04:04.29,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Gerald commands the military \Nstronghold of Coldwind Ridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.29,0:04:05.02,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,VALENCIA
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.29,0:04:06.86,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Timothy oversees the \Neconomic hub of Valencia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.77,0:04:08.52,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,PORT OF CLEARWATER
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.77,0:04:10.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Garcia controls the trade port, \NPort of Clearwater.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.72,0:04:11.52,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,SILVER CITY
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.72,0:04:13.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Tilly operates the cultural \Ncenter of Silver City.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.50,0:04:16.60,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,BORDER TOWN
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.50,0:04:16.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And I've been banished to \Nthis desolate Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.10,0:04:19.33,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, under these circumstances,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.33,0:04:21.71,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,what do you think my \Nchances of winning are?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.00,0:04:24.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's fine. You can be honest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.70,0:04:28.65,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Yes, each of Their Highnesses' domains \Nhave their own strengths.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.65,0:04:32.72,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,In comparison, it would be very difficult \Nto achieve anything in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.32,0:04:37.11,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Furthermore, considering \NYour Highness's past performance
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.11,0:04:39.98,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,and standing among \Nthe nobles in the capital,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.98,0:04:42.72,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,it's hard to see any real advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.46,0:04:44.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.27,0:04:48.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's why I need to find \Nanother way to impress Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.82,0:04:50.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, let me ask you this:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.35,0:04:53.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,who truly rules this kingdom?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.18,0:04:54.98,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Well, of course it is
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.98,0:04:58.50,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,the Royal House of Graycastle, \Nthe Wimbledons, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.50,0:05:00.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's just an illusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.06,0:05:04.41,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The true rulers of this kingdom \Nare not in Graycastle,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.06,0:05:04.97,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,THE ROYAL CAPITAL, GRAYCASTLE
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.60,0:05:07.02,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,THE HOLY CITY, HERMES
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.41,0:05:07.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.34,0:05:10.02,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The Holy City, Hermes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.02,0:05:13.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If only those crowned by the Pope \Nwere considered legitimate kings,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.58,0:05:16.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,then this secular regime is nothing \Nmore than a puppet of theocracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.45,0:05:19.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,No matter how prosperously \Nmy siblings govern their domains,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.20,0:05:21.73,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they ultimately belong to the Church.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.35,0:05:25.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If I can create a kingdom that \Nis not bound by the Church,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.82,0:05:29.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,then the throne will surely be mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.37,0:05:32.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, you've always been a loyal \Nsupporter of the Royal House.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.55,0:05:36.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You can't stand the Church's excessive \Ninterference in secular governance, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.46,0:05:38.56,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,You're right,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.56,0:05:41.13,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,but the Church's power \Nis deeply entrenched,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.13,0:05:42.70,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,and it has the people's support.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.70,0:05:44.34,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,What can we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.34,0:05:47.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The people's support for the \NChurch originates from its lies.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.18,0:05:49.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If we can prove the Church is lying,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.79,0:05:51.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they will no longer support it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.34,0:05:56.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,For example, witches aren't actually \Nthe embodiment of the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.06,0:05:59.64,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,So that's why you saved that witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.64,0:06:03.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, you've been the Assistant Minister \Nof Finance for twenty years, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.53,0:06:05.04,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.04,0:06:09.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If I win the Royal Decree, \Nthe "Assistant" in your title can be dropped.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.18,0:06:11.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Or possibly even further. For example,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.92,0:06:13.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,"Hand of the King."
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.16,0:06:15.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.92,0:06:17.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,do not question my decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.18,0:06:27.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,What did His Highness say?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.79,0:06:30.73,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.72,0:06:33.58,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Barov!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.20,0:06:36.04,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Did you even try to talk \Nsome sense into him?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.67,0:06:38.01,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Are you even listening to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.01,0:06:39.56,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Something's off about this witch business.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.56,0:06:41.59,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,It's not just this witch business.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.59,0:06:44.43,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,There's something wrong with \NHis Highness Roland himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.43,0:06:46.13,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yeah, something's wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.13,0:06:47.61,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This is serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.61,0:06:49.99,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,If the news leaks \Nand Hermes finds out,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.99,0:06:51.29,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,we'll be in big trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.24,0:06:54.72,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Hey, don't leave!\NExplain yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.64,0:07:10.95,Flashback,Anna,0,0,0,,Contract?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.51,0:07:12.56,Flashback,Anna,0,0,0,,I don't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.56,0:07:14.38,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,It's an agreement.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.38,0:07:16.63,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,Once you sign the last page,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.63,0:07:19.52,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,you and His Highness will be in \Nan equal employment relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.52,0:07:21.56,Flashback,Anna,0,0,0,,Equal... employment?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.99,0:07:26.09,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,Yes. His Highness specifically \Nemphasized this point: equal.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.09,0:07:27.44,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,You do work.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.44,0:07:31.56,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,His Highness pays you \None gold royal per month.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.67,0:07:37.58,Flashback,Anna,0,0,0,,That's... more than what \Nmy father earns in a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.44,0:07:39.56,Flashback,Anna,0,0,0,,Is there a mistake?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.56,0:07:43.01,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,Your pay was set by \NHis Highness Roland himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.01,0:07:44.45,Flashback,Barov,0,0,0,,There's no mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.45,0:07:47.00,Flashback_Italics,Anna,0,0,0,,Then... what does the prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.48,0:07:49.00,Flashback_Italics,Anna,0,0,0,,want me to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.61,0:07:52.30,Flashback_Italics,Anna,0,0,0,,Someone like me?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.34,0:07:55.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.81,0:08:07.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,How are you? \NDid you sleep well last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.05,0:08:08.68,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes, very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.68,0:08:10.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's great.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.08,0:08:12.01,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,After everything you've gone through,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.01,0:08:14.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you should've rested longer, \Nbut we don't have much time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.74,0:08:16.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'll make it up to you later.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.69,0:08:17.91,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.91,0:08:19.62,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I don't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.62,0:08:22.44,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness, why did you do this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.44,0:08:23.61,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.61,0:08:25.52,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Why did you save me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.52,0:08:27.81,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,And that contract...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.15,0:08:29.79,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,What do you want me to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.02,0:08:35.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's a beautiful afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.93,0:08:36.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Let's take a walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.84,0:08:37.65,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.20,0:08:50.25,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.27,0:08:53.80,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Why did you save me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.48,0:08:56.85,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I killed someone.\NI should be punished.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.40,0:09:00.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You mean saving your \Nfather's life from a bandit?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.04,0:09:02.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I think that's just self-defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.82,0:09:04.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You did what anyone would do.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.16,0:09:09.75,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,But even if you forgive my actions,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.48,0:09:12.03,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I'm a witch,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.48,0:09:15.34,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,the embodiment of the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.34,0:09:18.56,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,The original sin cannot be erased.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.63,0:09:31.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, this flower is for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.83,0:09:34.89,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.70,0:09:38.01,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,A citrus flower... It's beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.01,0:09:39.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.06,0:09:42.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But did you know the citrus \Nflower is highly poisonous?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.03,0:09:47.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Just kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.27,0:09:52.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,How could a citrus flower be poisonous?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.27,0:09:53.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Isn't that common knowledge?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.64,0:09:55.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yet when I said it was poisonous,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.72,0:09:57.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you instinctively let go of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.64,0:09:59.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The citrus flower is still \Nthe same citrus flower.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.15,0:10:00.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Its essence hasn't changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.93,0:10:03.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What changed is our perception of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.43,0:10:06.74,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,So you mean it's the same with witches?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.54,0:10:08.59,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.20,0:10:12.20,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,In my opinion, a witch's \Npower is like this flower.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.20,0:10:13.63,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Both are products of nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.63,0:10:15.15,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,They're neither inherently good nor evil.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.15,0:10:17.52,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,All this talk of the Devil and impurity,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.52,0:10:19.38,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,it's just people's opinions.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.38,0:10:22.38,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Since it's an opinion, \Nit can be changed, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.38,0:10:26.60,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness,\Nyour thinking is too simplistic.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.52,0:10:31.01,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,This power... is truly terrifying.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.24,0:10:31.68,Flashback - Top,Anna,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.31,0:10:35.02,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,The Church is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.69,0:10:39.13,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,A witch's power is the Devil's power.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.96,0:10:41.89,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Witches are the embodiment of the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.70,0:10:46.89,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,This power will kill \Neveryone who comes near me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.16,0:10:50.36,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,You should execute me immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.62,0:11:03.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If you're determined to die,\Nno one can stop you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.51,0:11:05.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Dying won't solve the problem, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.55,0:11:07.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's just avoiding it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.10,0:11:09.63,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Your father won't change \Nhis attitude toward witches.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.63,0:11:13.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And everything you've \Nlost won't come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.17,0:11:20.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Or you can choose another path,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.45,0:11:25.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and create a new world with me \Nwhere witches can live freely.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.20,0:11:33.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In that world, you won't \Nhave to live in fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.65,0:11:35.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You won't have to hide.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.18,0:11:38.99,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You won't have to hide your power \Nor be ashamed of your identity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.99,0:11:41.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Instead, you can choose the life you want,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.64,0:11:44.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and use your powers to benefit others.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.06,0:11:47.78,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In my opinion, that alone could \Nchange this suffering world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.78,0:11:49.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Just like this citrus flower,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.59,0:11:52.78,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,which symbolizes strength within hardship.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.29,0:11:56.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That can never be the Devil's power.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.31,0:11:58.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The contract I gave you
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.20,0:12:01.21,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,is a request for you to do this with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.35,0:12:06.93,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I want to go back to school,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.58,0:12:09.75,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,to read aloud with everyone \Nin the classroom,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.75,0:12:11.65,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,and to sing in the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.56,0:12:16.69,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,In future, I want to \Nbecome like Professor Karl,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.31,0:12:19.58,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,to be with children every day,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.37,0:12:22.54,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,teaching them to read and write.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.57,0:12:26.62,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.26,0:12:31.31,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Will that day...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.98,0:12:34.77,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,truly come?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.17,0:12:38.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It will.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.89,0:12:42.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As long as we work together.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.34,0:12:54.78,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I'm willing to give it a go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.70,0:12:57.39,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,What do I need to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.75,0:13:11.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,First, you must learn \Nto control your power.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.80,0:13:15.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,From now on, this will \Nbe your training ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.65,0:13:21.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You must completely master this power,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.65,0:13:25.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and control the temperature, \Nangle, and every other aspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.11,0:13:34.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But don't burn your clothes again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.97,0:13:36.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Or anything else, for that matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.25,0:15:01.63,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Last night, I reviewed last \Nyear's industrial reports
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.63,0:15:02.69,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and discovered that
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.69,0:15:05.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the only significant industry\Nin Border Town is mining.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.85,0:15:08.13,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Not only does this include building stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.13,0:15:11.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but also a substantial quantity of \Nmetal ores and gemstones.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.48,0:15:14.54,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Now look at this financial statement.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.54,0:15:16.81,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Last year's fiscal \Nrevenue was nearly zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.81,0:15:20.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Not only that, but trade records \Nshow only a few ore transactions
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.08,0:15:21.69,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and some deals for iron goods,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.69,0:15:23.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,all conducted with Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.25,0:15:27.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This meager revenue barely \Ncovers municipal expenses.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.85,0:15:30.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Most of the mining output \Nwasn't recorded at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.51,0:15:33.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There's also nothing on \Ndaily living expenses or taxes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.52,0:15:36.48,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Based on this, it seems Border Town \Nhas no agricultural production.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.48,0:15:38.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If everyone is engaged in mining work,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.79,0:15:41.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,how do they manage their \Ndaily food supply?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.09,0:15:47.34,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, did you spend all night \Nreviewing these reports?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.34,0:15:49.91,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,With so many reports, you must be...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.36,0:15:53.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes, it took a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.55,0:15:55.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I knew far too little \Nabout my domain before.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.84,0:15:57.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I left everything to you,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.62,0:16:00.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,while I indulged in revelry all by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.51,0:16:02.54,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. Thanks for your hard work.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.29,0:16:04.09,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.09,0:16:07.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,From now on, I will do what I need to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.22,0:16:08.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Please do your best to assist me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.76,0:16:14.16,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,I will obey your orders \Nand do my very best.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.98,0:16:17.84,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, actually, until last year,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.84,0:16:20.27,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,all ore produced in Border Town
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.27,0:16:23.36,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,was exchanged for food\Nwith Longsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.36,0:16:25.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Exchanged? Wasn't it sold?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.12,0:16:26.99,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,In the eyes of Longsong Stronghold,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.99,0:16:29.65,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Border Town is nothing more \Nthan their property.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.72,0:16:35.72,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,LONGSONG STRONGHOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.27,0:16:35.72,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,BORDER TOWN
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.65,0:16:33.67,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,They provide meager rations \Nto keep the workers going.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.67,0:16:36.61,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,You can hardly call \Nthem a trading partner.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.61,0:16:38.10,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Before your arrival,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.10,0:16:41.15,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,the original lord of \NBorder Town, Baron Boris,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.15,0:16:43.58,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,always obeyed the Stronghold's orders,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.58,0:16:48.22,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,handing over all ores to them\Nin exchange for meager rations.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.20,0:16:51.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Baron Boris... I remember him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.68,0:16:53.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,He was a weirdo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.58,0:16:55.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I came and seized his territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.20,0:16:57.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's understandable that he dislikes me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.93,0:16:59.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But logically speaking,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.43,0:17:01.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,since Border Town was his domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.60,0:17:03.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,even if it was for his own benefit,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.34,0:17:06.73,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,he should have wanted to \Ntrade the ores fairly, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.44,0:17:09.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,These ores are valuable.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.27,0:17:13.17,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Although Boris and his knights, \Nalong with several other nobles,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.17,0:17:15.78,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,are nominally lords of Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.78,0:17:19.10,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,they actually own property \Nin Longsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.10,0:17:23.78,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Their personal interests and businesses \Nare tied to Longsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.78,0:17:26.64,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,They never intended to manage Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.64,0:17:29.41,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,and are merely acting as \Noverseers for the Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.41,0:17:31.70,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,They couldn't care less about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.70,0:17:35.63,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,They're happy as long as they do their \Njob and exchange ores for food.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.63,0:17:38.81,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The Stronghold also gives \Nthem a share of the profits.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.81,0:17:41.66,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,It's an exaggeration \Nto call it an exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.66,0:17:44.07,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,No matter how much ore we give them,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.07,0:17:47.51,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,the food they give us \Nbarely keeps us alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.51,0:17:51.86,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The town's daily expenses still depend \Non that meager trade with Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.86,0:17:54.41,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The Stronghold doesn't \Ncontribute a single penny.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.48,0:17:58.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We can't carry on like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.02,0:18:02.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Cease all exchanges with \Nthe Stronghold immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.55,0:18:04.85,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,But what about our future food supply?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.85,0:18:07.02,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,BORDER TOWN
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.02,0:18:10.22,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,LONGSONG STRONGHOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.22,0:18:13.60,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,WILLOW TOWN
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.30,0:18:08.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Border Town will start genuine trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.08,0:18:11.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Sell all the ore already loaded onto \Nships to Willow Town for currency,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.60,0:18:13.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,then buy food directly there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.40,0:18:17.80,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,But what if Willow Town doesn't buy?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.80,0:18:21.46,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,After all, they've never handled \Nsuch a large ore transaction before.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.46,0:18:24.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We can sell to them at \Nhalf the market price.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.30,0:18:26.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,With such a large profit, \Nthey won't refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.56,0:18:27.81,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Half?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.81,0:18:31.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's right. We will immediately \Nobtain substantial start-up capital
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.60,0:18:33.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and quickly dominate the market.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.10,0:18:35.72,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,But at such a low price...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.72,0:18:37.21,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,What about the future?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.21,0:18:40.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In the future, we don't necessarily \Nhave to sell to Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.19,0:18:42.52,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,BORDER TOWN
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.18,0:18:42.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Look at this map, Barov.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.02,0:18:43.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Border Town is the source \Nof the Redwater River,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.02,0:18:44.31,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,LONGSONG STRONGHOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.68,0:18:45.24,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,which flows through the entire kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.10,0:18:46.19,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,WILLOW TOWN
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.24,0:18:48.88,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Once we have enough ships, \Nwe won't be limited to Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.40,0:18:48.23,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,REDWATER CITY
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.88,0:18:52.38,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We can navigate the Redwater River \Nand trade with the entire kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.69,0:18:52.77,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,SILVER CITY
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.38,0:18:56.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Redwater River will become \NBorder Town's Silk Road.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.27,0:18:56.19,Sign_Basic,SIGN,0,0,0,,ROYAL CAPITAL OF GRAYCASTLE
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.14,0:18:59.77,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,But Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.77,0:19:01.93,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Border Town doesn't produce silk.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.45,0:19:05.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That was just an analogy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.02,0:19:07.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In any case, we can use the Redwater River
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.53,0:19:09.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and comprehensively expand \Nour trading partners.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.75,0:19:16.11,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, although \Nexpanding trade is great,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.11,0:19:20.66,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,doing so would be like snatching food\Nfrom the Stronghold's mouth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.66,0:19:25.19,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,In that case, they probably \Nwon't take us in during winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.19,0:19:28.32,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Take us in? Why do we need to \Nspend winter in the Stronghold?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.32,0:19:31.60,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, how could you forget this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.60,0:19:34.43,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Winter brings the Months of Demons!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.93,0:19:36.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Months of Demons?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.43,0:19:39.50,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,After the first snowfall each winter,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.50,0:19:42.66,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,the Gates of Hell open within \Nthe Dragonspine Mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.66,0:19:45.67,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Animals from the Misty Forest \Nwest of Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.67,0:19:47.59,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,corrupted by demonic power,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.59,0:19:51.12,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,will transform into ferocious \Nand bloodthirsty demon beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.12,0:19:54.84,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,They surge forth in hordes from the \NMisty Forest, attacking eastward,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.84,0:19:57.58,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,leaving devastation in their wake.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.58,0:20:00.06,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Border Town has no walls.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.06,0:20:02.34,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,We cannot withstand the beasts' onslaught.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.34,0:20:05.48,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Therefore, every winter, \Nthe residents of Border Town
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.48,0:20:08.91,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,must evacuate to \NLongsong Stronghold for refuge.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.91,0:20:12.61,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Only the Stronghold's towering \Nwalls and elite knights
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.61,0:20:15.05,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,can withstand the demon beasts' onslaught.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.05,0:20:18.00,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Only after the beasts have \Nretreated the following spring
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.00,0:20:20.66,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,can the people return to Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.66,0:20:23.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Every winter, the residents \Nof Border Town must migrate.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.52,0:20:27.88,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,In other words, without solving \Nthe demon beast problem,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.88,0:20:32.19,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,it's impossible to establish a foothold \Nin Border Town, develop trade,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.19,0:20:33.81,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,resist the Stronghold,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.81,0:20:36.87,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,or even think about the ambition \Nof claiming the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.87,0:20:38.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Summon Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.08,0:20:41.00,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I've brought \Nthe men you requested.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.00,0:20:42.97,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,All of them have lived in \NBorder Town for over five years,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.97,0:20:44.98,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,and have experienced the Months of Demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.98,0:20:46.98,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,These two are the patrol \Ncaptains of Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.98,0:20:49.84,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Every year, they light the beacon fires \Nduring the Months of Demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.84,0:20:52.32,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This hunter claims to have \Nfought the demon beasts
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.32,0:20:54.33,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,and personally killed two.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.89,0:21:00.42,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What is the procedure for \Nlighting the beacon fires?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.42,0:21:02.09,Main,Greyhound,0,0,0,,Y-Y-Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.09,0:21:05.70,Main,Greyhound,0,0,0,,Y-Your... Your H-Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.21,0:21:09.21,Main,Greyhound,0,0,0,,If the demon beasts \Ncross the Misty Forest,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.21,0:21:11.35,Main,Greyhound,0,0,0,,we'd go and...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.98,0:21:15.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All right, don't be nervous. Relax.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.99,0:21:16.91,Main,Greyhound,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.64,0:21:18.73,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You speak for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.73,0:21:19.35,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.87,0:21:24.02,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Our patrol's outpost is located on\Nthe Dragonspine Mountain's southern slope.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.02,0:21:25.81,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,The Misty Forest lies at \Nthe foot of the mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.81,0:21:29.33,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Every late fall, our patrol closely \Nmonitors the Misty Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.33,0:21:32.39,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,When we spot any trace of demon beasts,\Nwe immediately light the beacon fires.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.39,0:21:36.00,Main,Brian,0,0,0,,Then we take a fast boat along the \NRedwater River and meet at the Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.00,0:21:39.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Fast boat? Wouldn't you get attacked \Nby demon beasts in the water?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.74,0:21:43.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Your Highness, the Redwater River \Nhas fierce currents and is very deep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.27,0:21:47.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In all these years, we've never recorded \Na single case of a demon beast crossing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.18,0:21:50.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Dragonspine Mountain's beacon towers \Nare very close to the river bank.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.64,0:21:53.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We're agile and usually aren't in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.80,0:21:56.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,How long are the Months of Demons?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.65,0:21:58.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Roughly two to three months.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.14,0:22:01.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Once it starts snowing in \NBorder Town, it won't stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.35,0:22:03.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The snow only melts \Nwhen the sky clears up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.59,0:22:06.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Months of Demons only \Nend when the snow melts.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.70,0:22:10.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The longest Months of Demons \NI experienced was two years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.73,0:22:12.91,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That one lasted nearly four months.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.91,0:22:14.29,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Due to starvation,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.29,0:22:16.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,many didn't survive that winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.63,0:22:19.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Starvation? But weren't you \Nin Longsong Stronghold?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.78,0:22:21.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Stronghold...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.87,0:22:25.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,They provide food based on \Nthe amount of ore we give.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.85,0:22:28.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If we ration carefully, \Nit lasts three months at most.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.98,0:22:30.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Food for a fourth month\Nwouldn't be provided
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.92,0:22:32.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,until another batch of ore arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.15,0:22:35.41,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But the Months of Demons \Nhadn't passed yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.41,0:22:38.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There was no way we could return \Nto Border Town to mine ore.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.85,0:22:40.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In that final month,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.64,0:22:44.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they watched us starve to death \Ninside Longsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.01,0:22:57.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You said you once killed two demon beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.13,0:23:00.16,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.16,0:23:03.20,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,I killed a boar-type and a wolf-type.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.20,0:23:05.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Boar-type? Wolf-type?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.81,0:23:07.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.02,0:23:10.10,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Demon beasts are mutated wild animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.10,0:23:12.78,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,The mutation amplifies some \Nof their primal instincts.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.78,0:23:14.41,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,The fiercer the animal before mutation,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.41,0:23:16.75,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,the more formidable it becomes afterward.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.75,0:23:20.00,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,For example, the boar-type has \Nincredibly tough hide on its back.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.00,0:23:22.64,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Even crossbows struggle to \Npierce it from 50 meters away.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.64,0:23:24.59,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,The wolf-type can run extremely fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.59,0:23:27.64,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,To kill one, you have \Nto set traps in advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.06,0:23:29.83,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The strong get stronger, \Nthe fast get faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.83,0:23:32.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But they're still just animals, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.00,0:23:33.17,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,That's correct,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.17,0:23:35.28,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,so they're not the most terrifying foes.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.28,0:23:38.12,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,The truly terrifying ones are the hybrids.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.12,0:23:40.22,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,They are the incarnations of demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.22,0:23:43.67,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Only Hell could create \Nsuch monstrous beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.67,0:23:44.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Hybrids...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.57,0:23:46.54,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Have you seen one?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.01,0:23:49.02,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,It has the strength of a lion,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.02,0:23:50.80,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,bears the wings of an eagle,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.80,0:23:52.49,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,and can fly short distances.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.49,0:23:54.13,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,It knows where you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.13,0:23:55.51,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,No matter how well you hide,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.51,0:23:59.17,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,it can find you with its keen \Nsense of smell and toy with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.17,0:24:02.88,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,It's as if it takes pleasure \Nin its prey's death throes.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.02,0:24:06.38,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There aren't many of \Nthese monsters, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.38,0:24:07.94,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.94,0:24:10.27,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,There are only two or three \Nin each Months of Demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.27,0:24:12.15,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Fortunately, even though they have wings,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.15,0:24:14.02,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,they can only glide at low altitudes.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.02,0:24:15.63,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,Otherwise, even the walls
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.63,0:24:17.68,Main,Iron Axe,0,0,0,,of Longsong Stronghold \Nwouldn't hold them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.23,0:24:24.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What's your name? \NWhy are you keeping your head down?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.54,0:24:25.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Raise your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.28,0:24:28.53,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,He's from the Mojin Clan.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.53,0:24:30.39,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,A Sand person in exile, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.41,0:24:32.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Sand person?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.52,0:24:34.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,No matter who you are,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.56,0:24:36.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,as long as you're in \NBorder Town, you're my people.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.32,0:24:38.40,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Raise your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.40,0:24:41.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Tell me your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.15,0:24:42.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,My name is... Iron Axe.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.25,0:24:44.75,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well done, Iron Axe.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.75,0:24:46.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Your courage will be rewarded.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.20,0:24:49.91,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Also, thanks to the rest of you \Nfor your service and intelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.91,0:24:52.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Each of you will receive \Nten silver royals as reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.80,0:24:53.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You may leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.59,0:24:56.39,Main,All,0,0,0,,Yes. Thank you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.97,0:25:02.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.64,0:25:03.33,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.48,0:25:05.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.53,0:25:06.70,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.72,0:25:29.09,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,Every winter, upon the first sighting \Nof traces of demonic beasts,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.09,0:25:31.43,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,the patrols light the beacon tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.64,0:25:43.22,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,Then, they rush down the mountain
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.72,0:25:45.98,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,to the nearest bank of the Redwater River.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.42,0:25:52.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, roughly how far would you say \Nit is from here to the river bank?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.20,0:25:54.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Roughly...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.18,0:25:56.56,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,around 2000 feet.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.88,0:26:01.29,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, forgive my directness,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.29,0:26:03.06,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,but why are you investigating this?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.40,0:26:07.95,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Don't tell me... you plan to \Nspend the winter in Border Town?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.95,0:26:08.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.52,0:26:10.99,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Not only will I not leave,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.99,0:26:13.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but neither will the 2000 \Nresidents of Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.27,0:26:15.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Everyone will spend the winter here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.52,0:26:18.38,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This... This is crazy, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.38,0:26:20.09,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,We only have a few dozen guards.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.09,0:26:22.29,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,How can we defend against \Nthe demon beasts' onslaught?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.29,0:26:25.06,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your castle can't fit over 2000 \Nresidents from Border Town!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.53,0:26:28.19,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Only Longsong Stronghold \Ncan hold all of us
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.19,0:26:30.21,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,and defend against the \Ninvasion of the demon beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.21,0:26:31.57,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Enough, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.57,0:26:33.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course I don't want to die here,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.53,0:26:35.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,nor will I abandon my people.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.97,0:26:37.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is our battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.23,0:26:39.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We will stand our ground here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.56,0:26:42.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We will crush the beasts \Nand defend Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.89,0:26:44.06,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.64,0:26:49.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I mean, we will defend against \Nthe demon beasts here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.20,0:26:53.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We will build the strongest wall here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.06,0:26:59.02,Sign_Basic,CREDITS,0,0,0,,Translator: Henry Lin\NTimer: Henry Lin\NEditor: Zachary Carlysle\N QC: William Haggard
